    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Dendritic growth poses a significant challenge in lithium-metal batteries, leading to degradation and\r\n potential catastrophic failure. To address this issue, a comprehensive understanding of dendrite\r\n formation is essential for devising effective mitigation strategies. In this report, we employ a linear\r\nstability analysis based on the Poisson-Nernst-Planck equations, which consider Li-ion transport\r\n while accounting for non-electroneutrality, and a transient base state, in a domain with and without\r\n a solid electrolyte interface. This approach suggests the switch from galvanostatic to potentiostatic\r\n charging regime. We propose using anisotropic electrolytes, high interfacial energy, and high SEI\r\n ionic conductivity to suppress dendritic growth. Such insights offer promising avenues for enhancing\r\n the stability and performance of lithium-metal batteries.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Tran, A. (2024). LI-METAL BATTERY MANAGEMENT STRATEGIES FOR DENDRITE SUPPRESSION USING LINEAR STABILITY ANALYSIS. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/kg394sc9320. https://doi.org/10.25740/kg394sc9320.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
